"[2609.00065] Scientific Agent Skills: A Library of Procedural Knowledge for Research Agents (https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.00065)\n\ue200cite\ue202turn11view0\ue201 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.00065\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 162\nL0: \ue200cite\ue2020\u2020Search\ue201 \ue200cite\ue2021\u2020Submit\ue201 \ue200cite\ue2022\u2020Donate\u2020info.arxiv.org\ue201 \ue200cite\ue2023\u2020Log in\ue201 L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search \u00b7 \ue200cite\ue2024\u2020Advanced search\ue201 L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Computation and Language\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 30 Aug 2026 (\ue200cite\ue2025\u2020v1\ue201 ), last revised 2 Sep 2026 (this version, v2)]\nL9: # Title:Scientific Agent Skills: A Library of Procedural Knowledge for Research Agents\nL10: \nL11: Authors:\ue200cite\ue2026\u2020Timothy Kassis\ue201 , \ue200cite\ue2027\u2020Vinayak Agarwal\ue201 , \ue200cite\ue2028\u2020Yuhuan He\ue201 , \ue200cite\ue2029\u2020Darshil Patel\ue201 , \ue200cite\ue20210\u2020Aubrey M. Brueckner\ue201 L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Scientific Agent Skills: A Library of Procedural Knowledge for Research Agents, by Timothy Kassis and 4 other authors\nL14: \nL15: \ue200cite\ue20211\u2020View PDF\ue201 \ue200cite\ue20212\u2020HTML (experimental)\ue201 L16: > Abstract:A language-model agent asked to analyse an experiment will usually return working code. Whether the analysis is defensible is a different question. A defensible analysis depends on procedural choices: which test the field accepts, which identifier namespace is authoritative, and which caveats must accompany a result.\nL17: We present Scientific Agent Skills, an open library of 163 such procedures in 16 areas of practice, including genomics, cheminformatics, medical imaging, study design and scientific communication. Each skill is a directory built around a versioned, human-readable instruction file. An agent loads the file only when a task calls for it; the directory often also contains reference material and runnable scripts. We report no task-level evaluation and no host selection rate.\nL18: We measure two properties of the documentation corpus: the always-resident descriptions of all 163 skills cost 7.1% of a 200,000-token window, and the median documented workflow fits within 23.9% of it, although 29 of 46 would overflow if every reference file were loaded. Openly licensed and available at \ue200cite\ue20213\u2020this https URL\u2020github.com\ue201 .\nL19: Comments:  | 31 pages, 16 figures, 2 tables, 1 listing. v2: adds a figure of how the documented workflows compose skills, quotes the skill clauses behind the introduction's examples, replaces the appendix listing with a procedural skill, names supported hosts and the pinned install path, and reports the two corpus findings in the abstract\nL20: Subjects:  | Computation and Language (cs.CL); Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI)\nL21: Cite as:  | \ue200cite\ue20214\u2020arXiv:2609.00065\ue201 [cs.CL]\nL22: \u00a0  | (or \ue200cite\ue20215\u2020arXiv:2609.00065v2\ue201 [cs.CL] for this version)\nL23: \u00a0  | \ue200cite\ue20216\u2020https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2609.00065\u2020doi.org\ue201 arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL24: ## Submission history\nL25: \nL26: From: Timothy Kassis [\ue200cite\ue20217\u2020view email\ue201 ]\nL27: \ue200cite\ue2025\u2020[v1]\ue201 Sun, 30 Aug 2026 15:40:35 UTC (2,386 KB)\nL28: [v2] Wed, 2 Sep 2026 21:50:40 UTC (2,995 KB)\nL29: \nL30: Full-text links:\nL31: \nL32: ## Access Paper:\nL33: \nL34: View a PDF of the paper titled Scientific Agent Skills: A Library of Procedural Knowledge for Research Agents, by Timothy Kassis and 4 other authors\nL35: \nL36:   * \ue200cite\ue20211\u2020View PDF\ue201 L37:   * \ue200cite\ue20212\u2020HTML (experimental)\ue201 L38:   * \ue200cite\ue20218\u2020TeX Source\ue201 L39: 